Stephen Schayer 
Director of Physical Hazards and Others 
OHSA Directorate of Standards 
Docket No. OSHA-2021-0009 
 
Dear Mr. Schayer: 
 
I am writing regarding the Heat Injury and Illness Prevention in Outdoor and Indoor Work 
Settings suggested requirements under review. 
 
At Coach USA we take every single precaution in assuring first and foremost that all our 
employees are working in the safest possible environment.  To ensure this, we have continual 
training that exceeds traditional programs and protocols in this regard. As our bus operators all 
drive in air-conditioned coaches, and all our facilities too provide each employee with working 
conditions that inhibit long exposure to heat conditions, we believe we exceed any new 
requirements. However, there are practical operational issues that may arise from them. For 
example, in New York City, there are idling laws which prohibit idling from occurring for longer 
than three minutes. The requirement of said policy would create a conflict with said law. 
 
We urge the agency to rethink this as in the case of Coach USA, our efforts coincide with the 
intended policy but with causing impediments to our ability to meet the needs of our commuters.  
 
Respectfully submitted.   
 
Sincerely, 
 
 
Dan Rodriguez 
