Dear Dr. Schayer: On behalf of the Subcommittee on Climate, Emergencies, and Disasters 
(SCED) of the President’s Task Force on Environmental Health Risks and Safety Risks to 
Children (Task Force), we write to share the SCED’s recommendations concerning the above 
proposed rule.  
The Task Force is a federal interagency body that was formed by Executive Order in 1997 and 
operates under the leadership of the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services and the U.S. 
Environmental Protection Agency.1 The SCED, as part of this Task Force, is comprised of 
approximately 50 federal staff representing eleven federal agencies and departments.2 The 
SCED’s recommendations reflect the commitment of its members to support federal efforts in 
addressing the impacts of climate change, emergency events and disasters on children’s (and 
relatedly pregnant and lactating women’s) health. Please note that the views expressed reflect the 
collective views of SCED and may not necessarily represent the views of every individual SCED 
member or their respective agencies or departments.  
SCED Comments and Recommendations on NPRM 
Provide more emphasis on the specific needs of children and youth:  The Notice of Proposed 
Rulemaking (NPRM) (p. 71042) states that “[b]ecause workers in the industries covered by this 
 
